Subject: [PATCH] Preserve restrictive row-security policy mode during reconstruction

FEATURE: Sec1
Upstream-Base: f1728591d33bd13d113d2a8d66bb99c377c31116
Bootstrap-Base: 624ad5a762581b5908a0e38e44a7c3477aeb9535

CreatePolicyCommandForPolicy is shared by immediate policy propagation and
table/metadata reconstruction. Emit AS RESTRICTIVE only for a restrictive
RowSecurityPolicy, retaining the exact existing output for permissive policies.
The actual fork source already contains this correction; its image compiles
that source, so this artifact must not be applied a second time to the fork.

Extend the existing RLS and metadata-sync regressions with observed policy
modes, invoker-role reads on physical placements, and real recreation.
The appended expected blocks come from actual PostgreSQL17.11 corrected
runs under a disclosed private2% disk-reserve fixture, with move-space checks
enabled. Every incumbent expected byte is retained. No product default changes.
Build/runtime evidence and its limits are recorded separately; this patch
does not claim upstream acceptance or broader distributed product readiness.
---
